========================================================================
 ALPHA-LATTICE / MEAN-FIELD GAP AUDIT
========================================================================

For n<=6: H = 1 + 2*alpha_1 + 4*alpha_2 exactly.
The free mean-field envelope at fixed alpha_1=m is 0 <= alpha_2 <= C(m,2).
The realized tournament lattice is much thinner.

n=5
  Distinct H values: [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13, 15]
  Achievable alpha_2 fibers at fixed alpha_1:
    alpha_1= 0: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,0]
    alpha_1= 1: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,0]
    alpha_1= 2: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,1]
    alpha_1= 4: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,6]
    alpha_1= 5: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,10]
    alpha_1= 6: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,15]
    alpha_1= 7: alpha_2 in [0]  | mean-field envelope [0,21]
  Spectral -> interaction fibers (c3,c5) -> alpha_2:
    (c3,c5)=( 0, 0) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 1, 0) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 2, 0) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 3, 1) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 4, 1) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 4, 2) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 4, 3) -> alpha_2 in [0]
    (c3,c5)=( 5, 2) -> alpha_2 in [0]

